From e16fd2797029676902f09e98ba9b33846fe1efa9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hashemamiri <hashemamiri804@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 06:30:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v45.4): host the untouched standalone formula editor
 from 66.html in a WebView dialog

- Replace the native Compose formula editor (pad/library/matrix/box) with the
  standalone editor page extracted byte-for-byte (code for code, zero edits) from
  the MATH_EDITOR_HTML string of 66.html: app/src/main/assets/math_editor_standalone.html
  (624,209 bytes, SHA-256 aae5777f9fb8705ccb2ed4a7c52e426e44ab45c7280055f936ed0aff4e917ceb).
- New MathEditorWebViewDialog.kt: isolated WebView + Android bridge; same signature
  (initialTex, onDismiss, onInsert) as the old FormulaEditorDialog, so ExamBuilderScreen
  only swaps the import/name. FormulaTarget and viewModel.insertFormula untouched.
- Bridge protocol mirrors the 66.html host: seed qTxt_1 with $tex$ (or $$), select it,
  openMath('qTxt_1'), wrap mfApply/closeMath at apply time only; apply => onInsert(tex),
  plain close => onDismiss. Verified with a jsdom end-to-end simulation against the
  real extracted page (apply fires exactly one APPLY event; cancel fires CLOSED).
- Display/PDF rendering stays native: NativeFormulaView, NativeMathText, NativeMathAst,
  NativeMathSvg/CanvasRenderer, NativeMathFormatter, NativeNaturalMathConverter,
  FormulaTextCodec, OfficialPdfPrintAdapter, PdfExamRenderer unchanged.
- Removed editor-only sources: FormulaEditorDialog, FormulaSmartHubDialog, FormulaLibraryDialog,
  FormulaLibraryNavigator, FormulaReferenceLibrary, FormulaReferenceStore, FormulaSmartReference,
  FormulaBoxEditor, FormulaMatrixFactory, formula_library_v13.json + their unit tests.
- V19InteractionTest updated to assert the WebView host + asset presence.
- Asset marked binary in .gitattributes so git diff --check can never flag the
  byte-identical page (trailing whitespace is authentic).
- docs: HANDOFF section 90 + MATH_EDITOR_WEBVIEW_V45_4_FA.md
